      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Generally, modern historical analysis views the UN as a necessary but often limited force in 21st-century conflict prevention. While the UN has successfully managed and stabilized certain political crises and provided essential humanitarian support, it often struggles against powerful state interests and the rise of non-state actors. Its effectiveness is often seen as highly context-dependent, sometimes succeeding in de-escalation and other times being politically paralyzed by the veto power among its most powerful members.",
